1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Finn was my father's uncle and he was always described as a Peer Gynt type, which means he was a bit of a trickster and an adventurer.  After finishing business school, he went to Germany and Canada and eventually 
2 CONC to Papua New Guinea, where he married an Australian.  He was working in Antwerp in the 1930s and came home to Norway.  His children were born in Antwerp.
2 CONT
2 CONT In a letter to Marge's long lost Australian family, Mali Viken described her uncle Finn as "a very charming man."
2 CONT
2 CONT At the end of the war, he had gone to northern Norway to work.  He caught some kind of lung infection and died.  His embalmed body was shipped to Oslo by train.  His half sister (Hanna Charlotte Weibust) went to the station to cla
2 CONC im the coffin.  She said there was a tuft of his hair sticking out from under the coffin lid.  Even in the death, he was chaotic.
2 CONT
2 CONT He apparently arrived in NYC on NAL SS Bergensfjord on Nov. 5, 1926.
2 CONT
2 CONT In July 1926, he was subject to a forced auction (tvangsauktion). He appears to have pawned his car.  That may have prompted him to leave Norway. In July 1925, his father had created a new car rental business Billigbil for him and
2 CONC  his brother Gunnar.  He may have pawned a car from that business.
2 CONT
2 CONT birth notice.  born in Bestum, Oslo. http://urn.nb.no/URN:NBN:no-nb_digavis_aftenposten_null_null_19000529_41_388_3
