1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Peder Anker, Count of Wedel-Jarlsberg served as Lord Chamberlain for King Haakon VII of Norway from 1931 to 1945 and was one of the King's closest confidants for over thirty years. He was a feudal count (''lensgrev
2 CONC e''), the highest rank of the Danish and Norwegian nobility and equivalent to Duke in most other European countries.
